WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions describe only what is on screen. This is not a product recording:
it is the open verification engine run from a terminal, 2026-08-06, one
continuous take, no cuts. Every hash, verdict and exit code in frame is
produced by the run you are watching. The tape that reproduces this exact
film is published with the engine.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.250
One command. No network, no model,
no dependencies.

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:06.230
Act one — a raw Bolt.new export
reaches the gates.

3
00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:08.850
DENY. It builds a production database
connection in shipped code.

4
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.950
Act two — credential material found
in the artifact.

5
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.580
Not blocked. Escalated to a named human,
and the approval binds to this exact hash.

6
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.500
Act three — the remediated artifact.

7
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.140
Every gate passes. A deploy token is issued,
bound to this bundle and no other.

8
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:23.450
Act four — the same artifact verified
one hundred times.

9
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:25.200
Paths, timestamps, permissions, locale,
time zone, process identity: all varied.

10
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.200
Then the negative controls — a changed byte,
a rename, an edited policy must move the hash.

11
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.200
They do. Determinism holds across one hundred
adversarially perturbed runs.
